  "content": {
    "id": "p37-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "A fair die is rolled four times. Find the probability of getting:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p37-q8-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "no sixes",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{625}{1296}$",
          "worked": "Let $X$ be the number of sixes in four independent rolls, with success probability $\\frac16$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(X=0)&=\\binom40\\left(\\frac16\\right)^0\\left(\\frac56\\right)^4\\\\P(X=0)&=\\frac{625}{1296}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      },
      {
        "id": "p37-q8-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "exactly one six",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{125}{324}$",
          "worked": "Let $X$ be the number of sixes in four independent rolls, with success probability $\\frac16$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(X=1)&=\\binom41\\left(\\frac16\\right)\\left(\\frac56\\right)^3\\\\P(X=1)&=\\frac{500}{1296}\\\\P(X=1)&=\\frac{125}{324}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      },
      {
        "id": "p37-q8-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "at least one six",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{671}{1296}$",
          "worked": "Let $X$ be the number of sixes in four independent rolls, with success probability $\\frac16$. Use the complement of no sixes.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(X\\ge1)&=1-P(X=0)\\\\P(X\\ge1)&=1-\\left(\\frac56\\right)^4\\\\P(X\\ge1)&=1-\\frac{625}{1296}\\\\P(X\\ge1)&=\\frac{671}{1296}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p37-q8-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "at least two sixes.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{19}{144}$\n\nSubtract the probabilities of no sixes and exactly one six from $1$.",
          "worked": "Let $X$ be the number of sixes in four independent rolls, with success probability $\\frac16$. Use the complement of fewer than two sixes.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(X\\ge2)&=1-P(X=0)-P(X=1)\\\\P(X\\ge2)&=1-\\left(\\frac56\\right)^4-\\binom41\\left(\\frac16\\right)\\left(\\frac56\\right)^3\\\\P(X\\ge2)&=1-\\frac{625}{1296}-\\frac{500}{1296}\\\\P(X\\ge2)&=\\frac{171}{1296}\\\\P(X\\ge2)&=\\frac{19}{144}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      }
    ]
  },
